---
// Food-code and category results: the first section until a run is graded, a supplement afterwards.
import { runs, fmt, modelName, params, href } from "../lib/data";
interface Props { num: number; T: Record<string, number>; n: number }
const { num, T, n } = Astro.props;
const direct = runs("direct_v2").filter((r) => !r.precision_of);
const byCodes = [...direct].sort((a, b) => (b.wweia_f1 ?? 0) - (a.wweia_f1 ?? 0));
const ROWS = 10;   // rows shown before the "show all" control, as in the other long tables
const cols: [string, string, (r: any) => any, (r: any) => string, string?][] = [
  ["WWEIA category F1", "wweia_f1", (r) => r.wweia_f1, (r) => fmt.f(r.wweia_f1), "wweia_f1_ci"],
  ["Food code F1", "code_f1", (r) => r.code_f1, (r) => fmt.f(r.code_f1), "code_f1_ci"],
  ["ASA24 lines matched", "component_recall", (r) => r.component_recall, (r) => fmt.f(r.component_recall), "component_recall_ci"],
  ["Preparation agreement", "preparation_agreement", (r) => r.preparation_agreement, (r) => fmt.f(r.preparation_agreement)],
];
const sub = (...parts: (string | null | undefined)[]) => parts.filter(Boolean).join(" · ");
const rankText = (r: any, col = "wweia_f1") => r[`${col}_rank_ci`] ? (r[`${col}_rank_ci`][0] === r[`${col}_rank_ci`][1] ?
  `${r[`${col}_rank_ci`][0]}` : `${r[`${col}_rank_ci`][0]}–${r[`${col}_rank_ci`][1]}`) : "–";
---
  <h2 id="codes">{num}. {num === 1 ? "Food identification by model" : "Supplemental food-code and category results"}</h2>
  <p>These comparisons use exact Food and Nutrient Database for Dietary Studies (FNDDS) codes or broader What We
    Eat in America (WWEIA) categories. F1 combines the share of listed foods matching a record line with the
    share of recorded dishes found, from 0 to 1. "ASA24 lines matched" is the share paired one-to-one with
    predictions. These code-based measures also cover runs that have not completed grading.</p>
  <p>Intervals are calculated by repeatedly drawing participants with replacement and keeping each person's
    photos together. The measures and interval calculations are described in{" "}
    <a href={href("methods/#measures")}>Methods, sections 6 and 7</a>.{T.amount && <>
    Amount estimates are reported in <a href="#amount">Table {T.amount}</a>.</>}</p>
  {direct.length === 0 ? <p class="note">No completed runs are available yet.</p> : (
  <p class="caption" id="table-codes-caption"><b>Table {T.codes}.</b> Estimates from a before photo or package front, compared with ASA24 records
        ({fmt.n(n)} photos per run). Food-code and category F1 and the share of ASA24 lines matched are means across
        photos. F1 combines the share of listed foods matching the record with the share of recorded dishes found.
        Preparation agreement checks preparation words on matched lines. Larger values mean more agreement.
        Values below the means are 95% intervals from resampling participants. Rank ranges cover the middle 95%
        of ranks by WWEIA category F1; overlapping ranges leave the order uncertain.
        Rows start with the highest WWEIA category F1; column headings change the order.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table data-sortable class="cards" aria-labelledby="table-codes-caption" data-limit={ROWS}
      data-more={`Show all ${byCodes.length} models`} data-less={`Show first ${ROWS}`} data-shown={`${ROWS} shown`}>
      <thead><tr>
        <th><button class="sort" data-first="asc">Model</button></th>
        <th class="n"><button class="sort" data-first="asc">Range of ranks</button></th>
        {cols.map(([label], i) => <th class="n" aria-sort={i === 0 ? "descending" : undefined}><button class="sort">{label}</button></th>)}
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {byCodes.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <td data-v={modelName(r)}><a href={`https://huggingface.co/${r.hf_repo}`}>{modelName(r)}</a>
              <span class="sub">{sub(r.developer, `${params(r)} billion model parameters`, r.weights_dtype)}</span></td>
            <td class="n" data-label="Rank range" data-v={r.wweia_f1_rank ?? ""}>{rankText(r, "wweia_f1")}</td>
            {cols.map(([label, , v, show, ci]) => (
              <td class="n" data-label={label} data-v={v(r) ?? ""}>{show(r)}{ci && r[ci] && <span class="ci">{fmt.ci(r[ci])}</span>}</td>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>)}
  <p class="note">Model weight formats use different numbers of bits to store a model's parameters. A mixture-of-experts
    model selects groups of parameters, called experts, for each text token (a word or part of a word).
    "Active" is the language-model count per token; an unavailable count is labeled. Counting rules, formats
    and run settings are described in{" "}
    <a href={href("methods/#models")}>Methods, section 4</a>. Table data: <a href={href("data/leaderboard.csv")}>leaderboard.csv</a>.</p>


